WEBVTT

00:00:01.140 --> 00:00:05.150
My name is Hidaka Sana. I'm a 16 year old in Year 2 of high school.

00:00:05.150 --> 00:00:09.710
Immediately after transferring, I was chosen to become a class rep, no thanks to Shuu.

00:00:09.710 --> 00:00:17.160
Luckily, I met Hoshino-san from the class next door at the library, and she's helped me out a lot.

00:00:17.160 --> 00:00:22.370
Hoshino-san is caring and gentle. She's a really nice girl!

00:00:22.370 --> 00:00:25.330
Nanaka used to be like that as well.

00:00:25.920 --> 00:00:29.340
It'd be nice if I could return to those times.

00:00:35.460 --> 00:00:37.540
Hey, what are we gonna do?

00:00:37.540 --> 00:00:40.190
About what?

00:00:40.190 --> 00:00:42.140
About Sana and Nanaka.

00:00:43.270 --> 00:00:45.560
What about Sana and Nanaka?

00:00:45.560 --> 00:00:50.160
We can't leave those two like that forever, can we?

00:00:51.720 --> 00:00:55.340
Well, we certainly can't leave them as they are.

00:00:55.710 --> 00:00:59.130
That's right. As their friends, we can't leave them like that.

00:00:59.130 --> 00:01:01.820
So, what should we do?

00:01:01.820 --> 00:01:05.330
Yeah, what should we do?

00:01:08.810 --> 00:01:12.780
Cookies and Pebbles

00:01:11.320 --> 00:01:13.530
Huh, all of us are going to the Kotsuchi River?

00:01:13.530 --> 00:01:17.730
Yeah, we're going this Sunday. You're gonna come too, right?

00:01:19.380 --> 00:01:20.510
It's okay with me.

00:01:20.510 --> 00:01:23.980
I'll invite Nanaka too. It's been a while since the five of us had fun together.

00:01:23.980 --> 00:01:26.100
Eh, Nanaka too?

00:01:26.100 --> 00:01:28.400
Oh, I can't wait!

00:01:28.400 --> 00:01:31.390
Should I make lunch for everyone?

00:01:32.820 --> 00:01:36.680
There's plenty of fish in the river. There's no need to worry.

00:01:36.680 --> 00:01:39.220
You just have to prepare some rice balls and tea.

00:01:39.220 --> 00:01:43.830
Hey, Shuusuke. Are you sure we're gonna be all right with all that big talk of yours?

00:01:43.830 --> 00:01:46.040
Of course we'll be all right.

00:01:46.040 --> 00:01:50.380
I bought some great fishing rods with the money I saved from work during summer break.

00:01:50.380 --> 00:01:53.070
I could even fight demons with it.

00:01:53.070 --> 00:01:55.970
Have faith in my skills. It's decided then. Leave it to me!

00:01:55.970 --> 00:01:57.450
Really?

00:01:57.450 --> 00:01:59.570
Also, don't forget your bathing suit.

00:02:00.220 --> 00:02:02.860
Isn't it still a little early to be swimming in the river?

00:02:02.860 --> 00:02:06.330
Don't be silly. We'll be stopping by the spa on the way back.

00:02:06.330 --> 00:02:07.160
Spa?

00:02:07.160 --> 00:02:10.620
Ah! The one that was newly completed this year?

00:02:10.620 --> 00:02:15.350
Yeah. After having fun, we'll cleanse ourselves and relax at the spa.

00:02:15.350 --> 00:02:17.260
Oh, I see.

00:02:22.680 --> 00:02:23.500
Hey!

00:02:23.500 --> 00:02:24.670
You won't be able to catch me.

00:02:28.270 --> 00:02:29.660
Sorry!

00:02:40.540 --> 00:02:42.970
Is this yours, Nanaka?

00:02:42.970 --> 00:02:46.480
Sorry. I was looking the other way, and I accidentally...

00:02:46.480 --> 00:02:48.300
I'll pay you back later.

00:02:48.300 --> 00:02:50.030
You don't have to.

00:02:50.030 --> 00:02:52.720
It's not that expensive anyway.

00:03:22.250 --> 00:03:24.070
This is for me?

00:03:24.410 --> 00:03:27.870
Yeah. This is for the one I broke yesterday.

00:03:28.100 --> 00:03:30.870
So, is that why you were at the store with her yesterday?

00:03:31.960 --> 00:03:36.680
You know, you were with Hoshino-san at the shopping district yesterday.

00:03:38.030 --> 00:03:42.580
While I was wondering what kinda mirror I should get, I bumped into Hoshino-san.

00:03:42.580 --> 00:03:45.010
So, she gave me her opinion.

00:03:45.530 --> 00:03:46.870
I see.

00:03:48.130 --> 00:03:52.510
And about all of us going on that trip.

00:03:52.510 --> 00:03:54.280
You're coming too, right?

00:03:54.280 --> 00:03:55.770
Yeah, I'll go.

00:04:12.750 --> 00:04:14.960
<i>Kotsuchi River, huh?</i>

00:04:14.960 --> 00:04:18.960
<i>We used to play a lot there when we were kids.</i>

00:04:27.060 --> 00:04:28.270
Cookies!

00:04:28.270 --> 00:04:30.270
Did you make these, Nanaka-chan?

00:04:30.270 --> 00:04:34.270
Yeah, but this was my first time, so they're not very good.

00:04:43.880 --> 00:04:47.280
It's been a while, but I'll bake some cookies!

00:05:00.920 --> 00:05:02.350
They're here.

00:05:03.650 --> 00:05:05.720
Sana-chan, thanks for carrying the cooler.

00:05:06.250 --> 00:05:07.730
It was heavy, wasn't it?

00:05:07.730 --> 00:05:09.630
That much weight is fine.

00:05:09.630 --> 00:05:12.710
All right, so everyone's here then.

00:05:12.710 --> 00:05:14.580
Ah, wait a sec.

00:05:14.580 --> 00:05:16.530
Hoshino-san is coming.

00:05:18.090 --> 00:05:19.650
Asami is coming too?

00:05:19.650 --> 00:05:22.940
Yeah, it was when I met her at the shopping district.

00:05:22.940 --> 00:05:28.710
I heard that you two were classmates with her last year, so I mentioned the trip.

00:05:29.190 --> 00:05:30.790
Was it a bad thing to do?

00:05:30.790 --> 00:05:33.130
Well, it's not exactly a bad thing.

00:05:44.010 --> 00:05:45.700
I'm sorry.

00:05:45.700 --> 00:05:49.780
Since Hidaka-kun invited me, I accepted straight away without thinking.

00:05:49.780 --> 00:05:53.680
It's okay. The more the merrier.

00:05:53.680 --> 00:05:58.970
But I arrived late and we barely caught the bus.

00:05:58.970 --> 00:06:03.740
The next bus would've arrived soon afterwards. You didn't have to run like that.

00:06:03.740 --> 00:06:06.400
When I saw the bus coming I panicked.

00:06:13.360 --> 00:06:14.930
That's...?

00:06:16.660 --> 00:06:22.510
This? When I was shopping with Hidaka-kun, he said he wanted to buy something to thank me.

00:06:22.510 --> 00:06:24.850
I told him not to because I felt bad.

00:06:24.850 --> 00:06:28.670
But while browsing, I said this was cute and I might buy one for myself too.

00:06:28.670 --> 00:06:31.880
After I said that, Hidaka-kun bought one for me too.

00:06:32.660 --> 00:06:33.830
I see.

00:06:40.850 --> 00:06:44.150
That's all that bastard ever says.

00:06:44.150 --> 00:06:46.700
He should worry about himself instead of others.

00:06:46.700 --> 00:06:48.350
What the heck is that?

00:07:03.960 --> 00:07:05.520
This should be all right.

00:07:05.520 --> 00:07:08.210
Everything is so convenient now though.

00:07:08.210 --> 00:07:13.500
You can rent everything from BBQ sets to cookware here nowadays.

00:07:13.500 --> 00:07:19.480
There's a camp site right below. You can rent from the management office over there.

00:07:19.480 --> 00:07:23.310
But, they've cut down a lot of trees because of the camp site.

00:07:23.820 --> 00:07:28.150
Well, it's okay, right? Since it's become more convenient.

00:07:28.150 --> 00:07:29.410
Really?

00:07:29.410 --> 00:07:34.030
Oh, yeah, Sana. Last time, you wanted to make a camp fire here.

00:07:35.690 --> 00:07:39.290
But, since we didn't have matches or lighters...

00:07:39.290 --> 00:07:42.630
...you said, "We can make a fire by rubbing wood together."

00:07:42.630 --> 00:07:47.230
But after all that effort, he couldn't even make smoke.

00:07:48.220 --> 00:07:54.160
By then, the sun was setting, and we told him to give up, but he became even more stubborn.

00:07:54.160 --> 00:07:57.200
He was like, "I won't go home until I build a fire."

00:07:57.200 --> 00:07:58.630
It was such a problem.

00:07:59.760 --> 00:08:02.050
Hidaka-kun did something like that?

00:08:02.050 --> 00:08:03.440
That's kinda unexpected.

00:08:03.440 --> 00:08:06.390
He was a really stubborn kid.

00:08:06.390 --> 00:08:12.200
Koshien is the stadium in Osaka where the finals of the annual high school baseball tournament is held.

00:08:06.390 --> 00:08:11.110
If there was a national stubbornness competition, he'd definitely reach Koshien.

00:08:06.400 --> 00:08:12.200
m 0 0 l 500 0 500 69 0 69

00:08:11.110 --> 00:08:14.190
Hey, that's enough about the past!

00:08:12.200 --> 00:08:12.900
m 0 0 l 500 0 500 69 0 69

00:08:12.200 --> 00:08:12.900
Koshien is the stadium in Osaka where the finals of the annual high school baseball tournament is held.

00:08:14.190 --> 00:08:15.950
I give up! Let go!

00:08:21.740 --> 00:08:23.250
Shuu...

00:08:23.250 --> 00:08:24.550
Use this.

00:08:26.510 --> 00:08:28.630
Sana, this is...?

00:08:30.840 --> 00:08:32.880
You kept it all this time?

00:08:32.880 --> 00:08:34.310
Obviously.

00:08:34.310 --> 00:08:37.910
Actually, ever since you gave it to me, I've stored it away.

00:08:37.910 --> 00:08:40.160
I've never even used it once.

00:08:40.160 --> 00:08:43.140
But I brought it today, since you said that we were gonna be fishing.

00:08:43.370 --> 00:08:46.670
Then, do you still have the glove I gave you?

00:08:46.670 --> 00:08:48.920
Of course. I also stored it safely.

00:08:48.920 --> 00:08:53.300
I guess the only way to use one glove is to stow it away safely.

00:08:53.300 --> 00:08:54.510
Oh, shut up.

00:08:54.510 --> 00:08:56.380
I envy you two.

00:08:56.380 --> 00:09:01.190
I should have given a more lasting present.

00:09:01.190 --> 00:09:03.910
A cake is gone once you eat it.

00:09:04.180 --> 00:09:05.910
That's not true.

00:09:05.910 --> 00:09:08.130
Really? I'm happy to hear that.

00:09:08.520 --> 00:09:11.880
Even though it's not physically there anymore, the memory remains forever.

00:09:16.580 --> 00:09:18.570
That sounded a little conceited.

00:09:18.570 --> 00:09:19.530
It is conceited.

00:09:19.530 --> 00:09:20.700
Conceited.

00:09:20.700 --> 00:09:23.080
It's conceited either way.

00:09:23.080 --> 00:09:24.100
Very conceited.

00:09:28.370 --> 00:09:31.670
I've got another fishing rod. Anyone want to use it?

00:09:31.670 --> 00:09:33.100
I'll pass.

00:09:33.100 --> 00:09:36.260
Say Shuu-chan, that one doesn't use bugs, right?

00:09:36.260 --> 00:09:37.520
Yeah, that's right.

00:09:37.520 --> 00:09:39.730
Then, I'll use it!

00:09:51.000 --> 00:09:55.250
Just do it like that, got it?

00:09:56.030 --> 00:09:57.810
Then, give it a shot.

00:10:05.740 --> 00:10:08.390
What? What's wrong?

00:10:08.390 --> 00:10:10.470
Don't pull!

00:10:10.470 --> 00:10:12.810
Aoi-chan. Put down the rod.

00:10:12.810 --> 00:10:14.590
What rod?

00:10:14.590 --> 00:10:16.360
Sana, something's pulling.

00:10:17.190 --> 00:10:18.530
Pull, pull!

00:10:18.530 --> 00:10:19.830
Eh? Pull?

00:10:19.830 --> 00:10:22.430
Don't pull! Don't pull!

00:10:22.430 --> 00:10:23.820
Pull! Pull!

00:10:23.820 --> 00:10:25.380
Pull?

00:10:25.380 --> 00:10:27.200
Don't pull! Don't pull!

00:10:27.200 --> 00:10:28.630
Pull! Pull!

00:10:28.630 --> 00:10:31.190
Which is it?!

00:10:47.800 --> 00:10:49.960
Shuusuke!

00:10:49.960 --> 00:10:52.650
What's the meaning of this?

00:10:52.650 --> 00:10:59.070
Well, how do I say it? Naturally, there are days when the fish don't bite.

00:10:59.070 --> 00:11:02.750
We wouldn't need people who mooch off taxpayers if we could settle it like that.

00:11:02.750 --> 00:11:05.660
Actually, we don't need them no matter what.

00:11:05.880 --> 00:11:07.090
Shut up!

00:11:07.090 --> 00:11:09.990
Sana, you're responsible as well.

00:11:09.990 --> 00:11:13.030
Don't try to be funny with that straight face.

00:11:13.030 --> 00:11:17.150
But, I managed to catch one.

00:11:18.360 --> 00:11:20.510
That's dirty, saving yourself.

00:11:21.310 --> 00:11:25.300
Either way, one fish isn't enough.

00:11:27.420 --> 00:11:29.200
Aoi-san, that's...?

00:11:29.200 --> 00:11:30.850
I prepared some BBQ!

00:11:31.410 --> 00:11:35.730
That's mean. You didn't believe in me.

00:11:36.570 --> 00:11:39.470
It's not like that.

00:11:39.470 --> 00:11:42.950
I just thought that you might not be able to catch any fish.

00:11:42.950 --> 00:11:45.500
Then, you didn't believe in me!

00:11:47.110 --> 00:11:50.100
Why? Why me?

00:11:53.430 --> 00:11:55.820
Will the fish be okay like this?

00:11:55.820 --> 00:11:57.680
Yeah, that's good.

00:12:31.720 --> 00:12:33.800
So, that's where you were.

00:12:33.800 --> 00:12:36.570
Don't run away from the BBQ preparations.

00:12:36.570 --> 00:12:40.040
For not catching enough fish, you should make up for it with work.

00:12:40.820 --> 00:12:42.130
Is something the matter?

00:12:42.640 --> 00:12:44.930
No, it's nothing.

00:12:48.970 --> 00:12:50.640
It's almost ready!

00:12:51.270 --> 00:12:54.300
Then, let's start with a toast.

00:12:57.250 --> 00:13:03.540
It may be a bit presumptuous, but allow myself, Wakatsuki Shuusuke, to do the toast.

00:13:03.970 --> 00:13:07.870
I remember five years back when my best friend Hidaka Sana-kun...

00:13:07.870 --> 00:13:10.710
Hurry, before the BBQ gets burnt.

00:13:11.990 --> 00:13:13.410
Then, cheers!

00:13:13.640 --> 00:13:16.380
'Then'? What the heck is that?

00:13:16.760 --> 00:13:19.280
Cheers!

00:13:27.080 --> 00:13:30.770
Man, if you're by the river, you have to have a BBQ.

00:13:32.200 --> 00:13:35.060
Here's the fish from Sana-chan.

00:13:35.060 --> 00:13:36.230
Thank you.

00:13:36.230 --> 00:13:39.780
I'm making some grilled rice balls now. I'll bring that later, okay?

00:13:48.410 --> 00:13:49.710
That was filling.

00:13:49.710 --> 00:13:54.050
You ate the most even though you didn't catch a single fish.

00:13:54.050 --> 00:13:55.390
Have you no shame?

00:13:55.390 --> 00:13:58.540
Now, if only there was some dessert.

00:13:58.540 --> 00:14:00.330
In that case.

00:14:07.180 --> 00:14:09.010
It looks so yummy.

00:14:09.520 --> 00:14:13.860
I felt bad because I was coming without properly telling you all.

00:14:13.860 --> 00:14:15.900
So, I made this.

00:14:15.900 --> 00:14:17.670
Is this homemade?

00:14:17.670 --> 00:14:19.020
That's incredible.

00:14:19.670 --> 00:14:20.930
Cut it faster.

00:14:20.930 --> 00:14:22.440
Don't be so impatient.

00:14:22.440 --> 00:14:24.350
What if I slip?

00:14:24.350 --> 00:14:26.690
You're turning there. The proportions aren't even.

00:14:26.690 --> 00:14:28.030
It is even!

00:14:30.720 --> 00:14:31.810
Nanaka.

00:14:32.890 --> 00:14:36.450
Asami baked enough for all of us. Come join us.

00:14:36.450 --> 00:14:37.830
Let's eat together.

00:14:37.830 --> 00:14:40.310
I'm fine. I'm already full.

00:14:49.320 --> 00:14:50.840
So, it's here?

00:14:51.230 --> 00:14:53.350
It's bigger than you imagined, right?

00:14:53.350 --> 00:14:54.090
Yeah.

00:14:54.090 --> 00:14:56.810
You'll be even more surprised after you go in.

00:15:02.590 --> 00:15:03.760
Just like I said, right?

00:15:03.760 --> 00:15:05.230
Sorry to keep you.

00:15:19.630 --> 00:15:21.140
This one is pretty good too.

00:15:28.380 --> 00:15:30.160
Well, I'm sorry.

00:15:30.160 --> 00:15:32.140
I'm the consolation prize for the boobs competition.

00:15:32.500 --> 00:15:34.710
Who? No one ever said anything.

00:15:35.060 --> 00:15:38.140
It's written all over your face even if you didn't say anything.

00:15:38.140 --> 00:15:40.180
Say, where's Nanaka?

00:15:40.180 --> 00:15:41.610
She's coming soon.

00:15:41.610 --> 00:15:42.690
Sorry to keep you.

00:15:53.140 --> 00:15:56.310
Well, it's not bad.

00:15:58.950 --> 00:16:03.680
What can I do? This is the only swimsuit I have.

00:16:15.990 --> 00:16:19.330
This isn't dangerous, is it?

00:16:19.330 --> 00:16:21.060
You'll be fine.

00:16:21.060 --> 00:16:23.400
Shuri and Hoshino-san already slid down.

00:16:23.400 --> 00:16:26.440
But everyone was like screaming.

00:16:26.440 --> 00:16:28.820
It's because they were having fun.

00:16:28.820 --> 00:16:32.660
There aren't any sharks at the bottom, right?

00:16:32.660 --> 00:16:35.910
No, of course not.

00:16:45.080 --> 00:16:46.250
Aoi-chan!

00:16:46.250 --> 00:16:47.640
Are you okay?

00:16:48.160 --> 00:16:50.190
That was fun!

00:16:50.190 --> 00:16:52.190
One more time!

00:16:52.190 --> 00:16:55.270
I think she's woken up.

00:16:55.270 --> 00:16:56.390
Seems like it.

00:17:05.720 --> 00:17:08.920
Aoi-chan, how many times did you go down the slide?

00:17:08.920 --> 00:17:10.960
I'm not sure, but a lot!

00:17:10.960 --> 00:17:13.450
And at the start, you were so scared.

00:17:13.450 --> 00:17:18.290
That's right. I wonder how many times she asked Sana if there were any sharks at the bottom.

00:17:18.290 --> 00:17:22.490
Don't lie! I only asked once!

00:17:24.490 --> 00:17:28.710
Oh, yeah, Sana. You've been wearing your wrist watch in the pool all this while, right?

00:17:29.040 --> 00:17:34.220
Yeah. It's waterproof. So, it's okay to use it in the pool.

00:17:34.550 --> 00:17:38.430
But isn't it difficult to swim with that since it's so bulky?

00:17:38.750 --> 00:17:41.220
I'm used to it, so it's okay.

00:17:41.220 --> 00:17:43.260
Can you take it off and show it to me?

00:17:43.260 --> 00:17:44.210
No way.

00:17:44.210 --> 00:17:46.080
Don't be so stingy.

00:17:46.080 --> 00:17:48.460
It's dangerous to hand it to you.

00:17:48.460 --> 00:17:49.940
What do you mean?

00:17:50.410 --> 00:17:52.800
It seems quite dear to you.

00:17:53.840 --> 00:17:57.610
Sana, is that a present from a girl?

00:17:57.610 --> 00:17:59.390
That's why you won't let me...

00:18:00.340 --> 00:18:02.160
What are you doing?

00:18:02.160 --> 00:18:05.200
I'm going to swim for a bit more.

00:18:22.970 --> 00:18:24.400
See ya, Sana.

00:18:25.310 --> 00:18:26.600
See you tomorrow.

00:18:27.000 --> 00:18:29.520
I really had fun today. Thanks.

00:18:29.520 --> 00:18:31.110
Bye bye!

00:18:36.850 --> 00:18:38.750
Hey, do you remember?

00:18:38.750 --> 00:18:43.130
That time at the river when you said that you'd make a fire to cook the fish.

00:18:43.130 --> 00:18:45.260
Please, no more of that.

00:18:45.260 --> 00:18:46.820
It's not that.

00:18:46.820 --> 00:18:51.340
In the end, you couldn't start the fire and everyone was starving, right?

00:18:51.850 --> 00:18:54.880
Then, Nanaka-chan gave cookies to everyone.

00:18:55.050 --> 00:18:58.570
I remember. Those cookies were really good, weren't they?

00:18:58.570 --> 00:19:00.600
Yeah, they were.

00:19:00.600 --> 00:19:03.890
I'd love to eat those cookies again.

00:19:04.250 --> 00:19:06.600
I have those cookies.

00:19:08.580 --> 00:19:12.740
I baked some cookies for everyone to eat.

00:19:12.740 --> 00:19:16.030
You should have told us earlier.

00:19:19.720 --> 00:19:23.020
Let's have some tea at my place then.

00:19:23.020 --> 00:19:23.780
Okay?

00:19:26.960 --> 00:19:28.830
Let's dig in then?

00:19:29.170 --> 00:19:35.240
It's been a long time since I've baked cookies. They won't be as good as before.

00:19:35.240 --> 00:19:38.670
So, they definitely won't be very good.

00:19:40.360 --> 00:19:42.310
This is really good.

00:19:42.310 --> 00:19:44.740
It tastes the same as last time.

00:19:57.220 --> 00:19:58.740
That was delicious.

00:19:58.740 --> 00:20:00.170
Oh, yeah.

00:20:02.250 --> 00:20:04.740
This is for the cookies.

00:20:16.520 --> 00:20:18.470
That's so pretty!

00:20:18.470 --> 00:20:20.200
Where did you get this?

00:20:20.200 --> 00:20:23.540
I found this in the river in the afternoon.

00:20:23.540 --> 00:20:26.790
How nice! I want one too!

00:20:26.790 --> 00:20:29.140
Sorry, this is the only one.

00:20:29.610 --> 00:20:31.730
Aww, that's a pity.

00:20:31.730 --> 00:20:33.600
It can't be helped then.

00:20:34.030 --> 00:20:37.150
It's a gift for Nanaka-chan after all, isn't it?

00:20:37.150 --> 00:20:41.650
But, it's just a stone I picked up from the river. It's nothing to be happy about.

00:20:42.010 --> 00:20:45.040
No, that's not true.

00:20:45.040 --> 00:20:46.620
I'm really happy.

00:20:53.020 --> 00:20:54.360
Yes?

00:20:54.360 --> 00:20:56.010
Ah, mum?

00:20:58.140 --> 00:20:59.440
School?

00:20:59.440 --> 00:21:01.340
Like I said, I'm going everyday.

00:21:02.040 --> 00:21:03.510
I sound lively?

00:21:03.510 --> 00:21:05.810
Did something good happen today?

00:21:05.810 --> 00:21:07.850
Yeah, kinda.

00:21:16.690 --> 00:21:19.990
<i>This is Sana's present to me.</i>

00:21:20.770 --> 00:21:22.810
<i>A gift only for me.</i>

00:21:25.350 --> 00:21:26.700
Everyone, good morning!

00:21:26.700 --> 00:21:29.580
Next episode; we met in brilliant destiny encounter.

00:21:29.580 --> 00:21:33.850
Shuusuke-san and I are in the front row of a great play with eyes of love.

00:21:33.850 --> 00:21:38.530
I'm definitely gonna get Shuusuke-san's heart with a strawberry jump shot.

00:21:38.750 --> 00:21:42.260
Next time on Myself; Yourself:
I'm Not a Child.

00:21:42.430 --> 00:21:48.330
With my evergreen charm, I give everyone a present of happiness with my shining star smile.

00:21:48.330 --> 00:21:50.060
Who are you anyway?

00:21:49.070 --> 00:21:54.950
I'm Not a Child

00:21:50.060 --> 00:21:52.360
It's something to look forward to in the next episode.

00:21:52.360 --> 00:21:54.490
Make sure you watch.
